   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) - Complete Guide\n",
    "\n",
    "LSTM is a special type of Recurrent Neural Network designed to solve the vanishing gradient and long-term dependency problems of basic RNNs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Table of Contents\n",
    "\n",
    "1. [What is LSTM?](#what-is-lstm)\n",
    "2. [Why LSTM?](#why-lstm)\n",
    "3. [LSTM Architecture](#lstm-architecture)\n",
    "4. [LSTM Gates Explained](#lstm-gates-explained)\n",
    "5. [Step-by-Step Working](#step-by-step-working)\n",
    "6. [How LSTM Solves RNN Problems](#how-lstm-solves-rnn-problems)\n",
    "7. [Mathematical Formulation](#mathematical-formulation)\n",
    "8. [LSTM Variants](#lstm-variants)\n",
    "9. [Applications of LSTM](#applications-of-lstm)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. What is LSTM?\n",
    "\n",
    "**LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory)** is a special architecture of Recurrent Neural Networks introduced by **Sepp Hochreiter and Jürgen Schmidhuber** in 1997.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Definition:\n",
    "\n",
    "LSTM is a type of RNN that uses special **gating mechanisms** to control the flow of information, allowing it to **remember information for long periods** and selectively **forget irrelevant information**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Key Characteristics:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Memory cells** - Store information over long sequences\n",
    "- **Gating mechanisms** - Control what to remember and what to forget\n",
    "- **Constant Error Carousel** - Prevents vanishing gradients\n",
    "- **Long-term dependencies** - Can learn patterns spanning 1000+ time steps"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Why LSTM?\n",
    "\n",
    "Basic RNNs have two major problems:\n",
    "\n",
    "### Problem 1: Vanishing Gradient\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "RNN Backpropagation:\n",
    "∂L/∂W = ∏(∂h_t/∂h_{t-1}) × ∂L/∂ŷ\n",
    "            ↓\n",
    "    ∂h_t/∂h_{t-1} < 1 for sigmoid/tanh\n",
    "            ↓\n",
    "    Gradient shrinks exponentially\n",
    "            ↓\n",
    "    Network cannot learn long-term patterns\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Problem 2: Long-Term Dependencies\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example:**\n",
    "```\",
    "\"The weather is nice today, so I will go to the beach and ___\"\n",
    "                                        ↑\n",
    "                            Need to remember \"nice\" to predict \"swim\"\n",
    "\n",
    "RNN: Fails because \"nice\" is too far back\n",
    "LSTM: Can remember \"nice\" throughout the sequence\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Solution by LSTM:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "RNN: h_t = tanh(W × h_{t-1} + U × x_t)     → Information overwritten\n",
    "\n",
    "LSTM: Uses Cell State (C_t) as a conveyor belt\n",
    "      Information flows unchanged through time!\n",
    "      Gates control what goes in and out\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. LSTM Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "LSTM has a more complex structure than basic RNN.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Components of LSTM Cell:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "                    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "                    │                                         │\n",
    "                    │     ┌─────────────────────────┐        │\n",
    "  Previous         │     │                         │        │\n",
    "  Hidden State ────┼────►│    LSTM CELL            ├───────►│  New\n",
    "  (h_{t-1})        │     │                         │        │  Hidden\n",
    "                    │     │   - Forget Gate        │        │  State\n",
    "                    │     │   - Input Gate         │        │  (h_t)\n",
    "  Current          │     │   - Output Gate        │        │\n",
    "  Input ───────────┼────►│   - Cell State          │        │\n",
    "  (x_t)            │     │                         │        │\n",
    "                    │     └─────────────────────────┘        │\n",
    "                    │                                         │\n",
    "                    └─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### The Cell State (The Memory)\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Cell State (C_t)** is the key innovation of LSTM. It acts like a **conveyor belt** that runs straight down the entire chain.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "    │                     CELL STATE (C_t)                │\n",
    "    │  C_{t-1} ════════════════════════════════ C_t       │\n",
    "    │      │                                     │       │\n",
    "    │      ▼                                     ▼       │\n",
    "    │  ┌───────┐     Gate Operations     ┌────────┐       │\n",
    "    │  │FORGET │ ◄───────────────────► │ UPDATE │       │\n",
    "    │  └───────┘                       └────────┘       │\n",
    "    │                                                     │\n",
    "    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Point:** Information can flow through the cell state **unchanged** (gradient = 1), preventing vanishing gradients!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. LSTM Gates Explained\n",
    "\n",
    "LSTM uses **three gates** to control information flow:\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.1 Forget Gate (f_t)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose:** Decide what information to **discard** from the cell state.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "    h_{t-1} ──┐\n",
    "             ├──► σ ───► f_t (value between 0 and 1)\n",
    "    x_t   ────┘\n",
    "\n",
    "    f_t = σ(W_f · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_f)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**How it works:**\n",
    "- Takes previous hidden state (h_{t-1}) and current input (x_t)\n",
    "- Outputs a number between **0 and 1** for each cell state element\n",
    "- **1** = \"completely keep this\"\n",
    "- **0** = \"completely forget this\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.2 Input Gate (i_t) and Candidate Values (C̃_t)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose:** Decide what new information to **add** to the cell state.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "    h_{t-1} ──┐\n",
    "             ├──► σ ───► i_t (input gate)\n",
    "    x_t   ────┘\n",
    "\n",
    "    i_t = σ(W_i · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_i)\n",
    "\n",
    "    h_{t-1} ──┐\n",
    "             ├──► tanh ───► C̃_t (candidate values)\n",
    "    x_t   ────┘\n",
    "\n",
    "    C̃_t = tanh(W_c · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_c)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**How it works:**\n",
    "- **i_t** - Decides which positions to update\n",
    "- **C̃_t** - Contains new candidate values to add\n",
    "- tanh creates values between **-1 and 1**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.3 Output Gate (o_t)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose:** Decide what **part of the cell state** to output as hidden state.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "    h_{t-1} ──┐\n",
    "             ├──► σ ───► o_t (output gate)\n",
    "    x_t   ────┘\n",
    "\n",
    "    o_t = σ(W_o · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_o)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**How it works:**\n",
    "- Decides what parts of cell state to expose\n",
    "- Hidden state (h_t) is then: h_t = o_t × tanh(C_t)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 5. Step-by-Step Working\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's trace through an LSTM cell step by step:\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 0: Initial State\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "Given:\n",
    "  - Previous hidden state: h_{t-1}\n",
    "  - Previous cell state: C_{t-1}\n",
    "  - Current input: x_t\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 1: Forget Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "f_t = σ(W_f · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_f)\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: If f_t = [0.9, 0.1, 0.8]\n",
    "         - Keep 90% of first memory\n",
    "         - Forget 90% of second memory\n",
    "         - Keep 80% of third memory\n",
    "\n",
    "C_{t-1} = [0.5, 0.8, 0.3]\n",
    "C_forgotten = C_{t-1} × f_t = [0.45, 0.08, 0.24]\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2: Input Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "i_t = σ(W_i · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_i)      # What to update\n",
    "C̃_t = tanh(W_c · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_c)   # New values to add\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "i_t = [0.7, 0.2, 0.9]\n",
    "C̃_t = [0.4, 0.6, 0.1]\n",
    "\n",
    "New memory = i_t × C̃_t = [0.28, 0.12, 0.09]\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 3: Update Cell State\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "C_t = C_forgotten + New_memory\n",
    "C_t = (C_{t-1} × f_t) + (i_t × C̃_t)\n",
    "\n",
    "C_t = [0.45, 0.08, 0.24] + [0.28, 0.12, 0.09]\n",
    "C_t = [0.73, 0.20, 0.33]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**This is the key to solving vanishing gradients!**\n",
    "- We use **addition** (not matrix multiplication)\n",
    "- Gradient can flow back unchanged!\n",
    "- Addition derivative is **always 1**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 4: Output Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "o_t = σ(W_o · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_o)\n",
    "h_t = o_t × tanh(C_t)\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "o_t = [0.6, 0.5, 0.7]\n",
    "tanh(C_t) = tanh([0.73, 0.20, 0.33]) = [0.63, 0.20, 0.32]\n",
    "\n",
    "h_t = [0.6, 0.5, 0.7] × [0.63, 0.20, 0.32]\n",
    "h_t = [0.38, 0.10, 0.22]\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Complete Flow Diagram:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "           h_{t-1} ──┐\n",
    "                    │\n",
    "           x_t ─────┤\n",
    "                    │\n",
    "                    ▼\n",
    "              ┌──────────┐\n",
    "              │ Forget   │──► f_t ──► (C_{t-1} × f_t)\n",
    "              │  Gate    │                 │\n",
    "              └──────────┘                 │\n",
    "                    │                      │\n",
    "                    ▼                      ▼\n",
    "              ┌──────────┐           ┌──────────┐\n",
    "              │  Input   │──► i_t ──►│          │\n",
    "              │  Gate    │           │  Cell    │──► C_t\n",
    "              └──────────┘    │      │  State   │\n",
    "                    │         │      │  Update  │\n",
    "                    ▼         ▼      └──────────┘\n",
    "              ┌──────────┐           ┌──────────┐\n",
    "              │ Candidate│──► C̃_t ──►│          │\n",
    "              │ Values   │           └──────────┘\n",
    "              └──────────┘                 │\n",
    "                    │                      │\n",
    "                    ▼                      ▼\n",
    "              ┌──────────┐\n",
    "              │  Output  │──► o_t ──► h_t = o_t × tanh(C_t)\n",
    "              │  Gate    │\n",
    "              └──────────┘\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 6. How LSTM Solves RNN Problems\n",
    "\n",
    "### Problem 1: Vanishing Gradient - SOLVED\n",
    "\n",
    "**RNN Problem:**\n",
    "```\n",
    "∂h_t/∂h_{t-1} = tanh' × W_h\n",
    "              = small_value × W_h\n",
    "              → Gradient shrinks exponentially\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**LSTM Solution:**\n",
    "```\",
    "Cell State Update: C_t = C_{t-1} × f_t + i_t × C̃_t\n",
    "\n",
    "∂C_t/∂C_{t-1} = f_t\n",
    "               = σ(W_f · [h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
    "               = 1 (when gate is open)\n",
    "\n",
    "Since f_t can be 1, gradient flows unchanged!\n",
    "This is called \"Constant Error Carousel\"\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Problem 2: Long-Term Dependencies - SOLVED\n",
    "\n",
    "**RNN Problem:**\n",
    "```\n",
    "All information is stored in h_t\n",
    "New information overwrites old information\n",
    "Cannot selectively remember\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**LSTM Solution:**\n",
    "```\n",
    "1. Separate memory (C_t) from hidden state (h_t)\n",
    "2. Gates control what enters memory:\n",
    "   - Forget Gate: Remove old irrelevant info\n",
    "   - Input Gate: Add new important info\n",
    "3. Cell state flows unchanged (conveyor belt)\n",
    "4. Hidden state is selective output from memory\n",
    "\n",
    "Result: Can remember relevant info for 1000+ time steps!\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Problem 3: Information Overwriting - SOLVED\n",
    "\n",
    "**RNN Problem:**\n",
    "```\n",
    "h_t = tanh(W × h_{t-1} + U × x_t)\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "New computation overwrites everything\n",
    "No control over what to keep\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**LSTM Solution:**\n",
    "```\n",
    "C_t = C_{t-1} × f_t + i_t × C̃_t\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "1. Multiply old state by forget factor (not overwrite)\n",
    "2. Add new information (not replace)\n",
    "3. Information accumulates, not replaces\n",
    "4. Gates provide fine-grained control\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Comparison Table:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Aspect | RNN | LSTM |\n",
    "|--------|-----|------|\n",
    "| Memory | Single hidden state | Cell state + hidden state |\n",
    "| Information Flow | Overwrites | Accumulates |\n",
    "| Gradient Flow | Multiplication | Addition |\n",
    "| Control | None | 3 gates |\n",
    "| Long Dependencies | Fails | Works |\n",
    "| Vanishing Gradient | Severe | Prevented |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 7. Mathematical Formulation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Complete LSTM Equations:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Given: x_t (input), h_{t-1} (previous hidden), C_{t-1} (previous cell state)\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Forget Gate:\n",
    "   f_t = σ(W_f · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_f)\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Input Gate:\n",
    "   i_t = σ(W_i · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_i)\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Candidate Values:\n",
    "   C̃_t = tanh(W_c · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_c)\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Cell State Update:\n",
    "   C_t = f_t × C_{t-1} + i_t × C̃_t\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Output Gate:\n",
    "   o_t = σ(W_o · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_o)\n",
    "\n",
    "6. Hidden State:\n",
    "   h_t = o_t × tanh(C_t)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Dimensions:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "If:\n",
    "  - Input dimension: d_x\n",
    "  - Hidden dimension: d_h\n",
    "  - Cell dimension: d_c (= d_h)\n",
    "\n",
    "Then:\n",
    "  - W_f: (d_h, d_x + d_h)\n",
    "  - W_i: (d_h, d_x + d_h)\n",
    "  - W_c: (d_h, d_x + d_h)\n",
    "  - W_o: (d_h, d_x + d_h)\n",
    "\n",
    "Total parameters: 4 × d_h × (d_x + d_h) + 4 × d_h\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Gradient Flow Comparison:\n",
    "\n",
    "**RNN Gradient:**\n",
    "```\n",
    "∂L/∂W = ∏_{k=1}^{t} (tanh' × W)\n",
    "       = ∏_{k=1}^{t} small_value\n",
    "       → Approaches 0 exponentially\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**LSTM Gradient:**\n",
    "```\n",
    "∂C_t/∂C_{t-1} = f_t = σ(W_f · [h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
    "\n",
    "Since f_t can be 1 (when gate is open):\n",
    "       = 1 (constant!)\n",
    "\n",
    "This allows gradient to flow unchanged!\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 8. LSTM Variants\n",
    "\n",
    "### 8.1 Vanilla LSTM\n",
    "\n",
    "The original LSTM with three gates (forget, input, output).\n",
    "\n",
    "### 8.2 Peephole LSTM\n",
    "\n",
    "Gates can \"peek\" at the cell state:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "f_t = σ(W_f · [h_{t-1}, x_t, C_{t-1}] + b_f)\n",
    "i_t = σ(W_i · [h_{t-1}, x_t, C_{t-1}] + b_i)\n",
    "o_t = σ(W_o · [h_{t-1}, x_t, C_t] + b_o)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8.3 GRU (Gated Recurrent Unit)\n",
    "\n",
    "Simplified version of LSTM with only 2 gates:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "1. Update Gate (z_t): Combines forget and input gates\n",
    "2. Reset Gate (r_t): Decides how much past to forget\n",
    "\n",
    "Equations:\n",
    "z_t = σ(W_z · [h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
    "r_t = σ(W_r · [h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
    "C̃_t = tanh(W · [r_t × h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
    "h_t = (1 - z_t) × h_{t-1} + z_t × C̃_t\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Advantages:** Fewer parameters, faster training, often similar performance"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Comparison:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Variant | Gates | Parameters | Performance |\n",
    "|---------|-------|------------|-------------|\n",
    "| Vanilla LSTM | 3 | High | Excellent |\n",
    "| Peephole LSTM | 3 | Higher | Excellent |\n",
    "| GRU | 2 | Low | Often equal to LSTM |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 9. Applications of LSTM\n",
    "\n",
    "### Natural Language Processing:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "✓ Language Modeling\n",
    "✓ Text Generation\n",
    "✓ Machine Translation\n",
    "✓ Sentiment Analysis\n",
    "✓ Text Summarization\n",
    "✓ Question Answering\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Speech & Audio:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "✓ Speech Recognition\n",
    "✓ Text-to-Speech\n",
    "✓ Music Generation\n",
    "✓ Audio Classification\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Time Series:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
